  "response": "To count embedding and LLM tokens in the current LlamaIndex setup, you should follow the updated approach using the `TokenCountingHandler` callback. Here's a step-by-step guide based on the provided context:\n\n1. **Setup LLM and Embedding Models:**\n   You need to initialize `MockLLM` and `MockEmbedding` objects for testing purposes. This is done as follows:\n\n   ```python\n   from llama_index.core.llms import MockLLM\n   from llama_index.core import MockEmbedding\n\n   llm = MockLLM(max_tokens=256)\n   embed_model = MockEmbedding(embed_dim=1536)\n   ```\n\n2. **Setup Token Counting Callback:**\n   Use the `TokenCountingHandler` to manage token counting. This involves setting up a tokenizer and a callback manager:\n\n   ```python\n   import tiktoken\n   from llama_index.core.callbacks import CallbackManager, TokenCountingHandler\n\n   token_counter = TokenCountingHandler(\n       tokenizer=tiktoken.encoding_for_model(\"gpt-3.5-turbo\").encode\n   )\n\n   callback_manager = CallbackManager([token_counter])\n   ```\n\n3. **Integrate with Global Settings:**\n   Assign the LLM and embedding models to the global `Settings`:\n\n   ```python\n   from llama_index.core import Settings\n\n   Settings.llm = llm\n   Settings.embed_model = embed_model\n   ```\n\n4. **Configure Tokenizer (if needed):**\n   If you are using a different LLM, ensure the tokenizer is updated to match the new model for accurate token counting:\n\n   ```python\n   from llama_index.core import Settings\n\n   # Example with tiktoken\n   import tiktoken\n   Settings.tokenizer = tiktoken.encoding_for_model(\"your-model-name\").encode\n\n   # Example with Hugging Face\n   from transformers import AutoTokenizer\n   Settings.tokenizer = AutoTokenizer.from_pretrained(\"your-model-name\")\n   ```\n\nThis setup allows you to estimate token usage for both LLM and embedding calls, which can help in predicting costs associated with index construction and querying.\n\nFor more details, you can refer to the example notebook provided in the documentation: [Token Counting Example Notebook](/python/examples/observability/tokencountinghandler).",
